<title>JAPAN: Japan October pork imports down 63.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan October pork imports down 63.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's pork imports in October totalled 41,751 tonnes, down 63.7 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>Details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Oct 96	 Sept 96	Oct 95</p>
<p> Total	     41,751	 28,229	 115,008</p>
<p> Refrigerated    15,404	 13,464	  20,318</p>
<p> Frozen	    26,347	 14,765	  94,690</p>
<p>Major suppliers of refrigerated pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Taiwan	     7,284	  7,093	  10,159</p>
<p> U.S.		 6,949	  5,303	   9,377</p>
<p>Major supplier of frozen pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Oct 96	  Sept 96	Oct 95</p>
<p> Taiwan	    16,901	  7,397	  31,829</p>
<p>Imports of refrigerated pork in the first 10 months of calendar 1996 totalled 145,385 tonnes, against 144,272 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>Imports of frozen pork in the first 10 months of calendar 1996 came to 432,789 tonnes, against 383,150 tonnes in the same period of 1995, ministry data showed.</p>
